  "verbalization": "Xestamine E is shown to have a target relationship with CD70 antigen, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Ebracteolatanolide A and Epicoccin C. These compounds are linked to DNA polymerase eta, suggesting a potential pathway through CD70 antigen. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Xestamine E may interact with DNA polymerase eta via CD70 antigen, which is a common intermediary in the targeting process. The scores from all three paths are consistent, suggesting a strong and reliable relationship. The mechanism appears to involve CD70 antigen as a bridge between Xestamine E and DNA polymerase eta, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a plausible mechanism, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between Xestamine E and DNA polymerase eta.",
